# netsurf: raise the precise-mark ring to 128 under a cost guard (patch 309)
# Generated 2026-10-19
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 308)
#
# Doc-20 stage 1. The stage-0 census (patch 308) showed real batches wider
# than the 32-mark precise ring (over=1 on a 40-mark burst) with per-mark
# local answers far below a full reconvert's cost, so the old ceiling was
# discarding wins. This patch raises the ring to 128 and adds a cost guard:
# marks are answered in order while the cumulative local cost stays below
# the content's initial conversion cost (the budget); if the guard trips
# mid-batch, the rest takes one full reconvert.
#
# The guard can only move batches TOWARD the full reconvert, never away from
# a safeguard: per-mark semantics are exactly patch 301's (same order, same
# defer-and-retry, same two-decline rule), and marks already answered stand
# (their local answers are complete; declines are non-destructive). The
# budget is the initial conversion's measured microseconds, per content.
# Reconverts do NOT refresh it: the RECONVPHASE accumulators are cumulative
# per navigation and do not bracket the real build work (sub-ms on pages
# whose rebuild is hundreds of ms), so a reconvert-derived sample would be
# garbage. The initial conversion is a full build, strictly more expensive
# than a reconvert, so the budget errs permissive -- the guard trips later,
# never earlier, than a true reconvert-cost budget would.
#
# BSS cost: 8 slots x 128 x 24 bytes = 24,576 bytes (was 6,144).
#
# Proof: a 120-mark burst (60 rows x textContent+className, past the old
# 32-mark ceiling) trips the guard on a 200-paragraph page -- the census
# shows the guard firing (FULLCAUSE total=2 local=1 guard=1: the innerHTML
# batch's local full reconvert plus the burst's guard trip). The guard
# tripped correctly in focused proof with a tight budget (12.5ms): 15 of
# 120 marks answered, then one full reconvert. On larger pages with bigger
# budgets the burst is answered locally; the guard is a backstop for the
# worst case, not a throttle on the win.
#
# The gate page JS-batch-burst.html (BATCHBURST) covers the guard leg --
# the census asserts total=2 guard=1. The local-answer leg is proven by
# the focused proof (120 marks answered locally when the budget allows)
# and the stage-0 census.
# < 1.48s budget), which is the correct behavior -- the guard bounds the
# worst case instead of merely raising the ceiling.
#
# Pre-existing issues noted during proof (not caused by this patch):
# - The 5000-paragraph tree does not fully rebuild on reconvert (partial
#   box tree, ~128 boxes); the DOM is correct and DOMSTALL passes 8/8.
#   Affects 307 and 309 equally.
# - RECONVPHASE accumulators read sub-ms on real rebuilds; not usable as
#   a budget source (hence the initial-conversion budget).
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run (no vitaSDK on this VM).
# Device expectation is in Doc 10.
